<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>A boda boda rider buys a motorbike for Ksh <m>{185\,000}</m>. It depreciates at <m>{17}\%</m> a year (reducing balance).</p><p>(a) Find its value after <m>{3}</m> years, to the nearest shilling.</p><p>Ksh <fillin characters="10" name="ans1"/>  </p><p>(b) Find the total depreciation.</p><p>Ksh <fillin characters="10" name="ans2"/>  </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Each year's loss is a percentage of what the item is worth at the start of that year, so the losses get smaller. Each year the value is multiplied by <m>1 - \frac{ {17} }{100} = {0.83}</m>.</p><p>(a) <m>V = {185\,000} \times {0.83}^{ {3} } = {105\,780.60}</m>, so the value is Ksh <m>{105\,781}</m> to the nearest shilling.</p><p>(b) Depreciation <m>= P - V = {185\,000} - {105\,780.60} = {79\,219.41}</m>, about Ksh <m>{79\,219}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>105781</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>79219</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>